- va, v b, and vc are the instantaneous three-phase
stator voltages;
- ia, ib, and ic are the instantaneous three-phase stator
currents;
- ea, e b, and ec are the instantaneous three-phase
back EMFs;
- R is the armature resistance;
- Lij (i = a, b, c and j = a, b, c ) are the mutual
inductances which are symmetrical.

EV propulsion requires the motor drives offering
four-quadrant characteristics for:
- forward motoring;
- forward regeneration;
- backward motoring;
- backward regeneration.
Particularly, the forward regeneration is essential
to capture the braking energy which in turn
charges the EV battery, leading to increase the
driving range per charge by over 10%.
